(5\) Lean Capital Requirement) Tj
T*
(Funding ask \(startup\): R280,000) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use of funds \(practical split\)) Tj
T*
(28% Safety gear, tack, and setup essentials) Tj
T*
(20% Horse care reserve \(feed, vet, farrier buffer\)) Tj
T*
(15% Insurance and compliance costs) Tj
T*
(15% Basic marketing + content + booking setup) Tj
T*
(12% Working capital buffer) Tj
T*
(10% Route/site preparation and signage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This budget is enough to start responsibly without creating scale pressure too early.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6\) Monthly Cost Discipline \(Target\)) Tj
T*
(Key monthly cost buckets:) Tj
T*
(Horse care) Tj
T*
(Guide/support wages) Tj
T*
(Fuel/transport) Tj
T*
(Insurance) Tj
T*
(Partner commissions \(if referred bookings\)) Tj
T*
(Marketing and admin) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Control rule: Keep fixed overhead low; use variable staffing around demand peaks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7\) Revenue Model \(Simple\)) Tj
T*
(Monthly revenue is based on booked slots only:) Tj
T*
(Scenic bookings  scenic rate) Tj
T*
(Sunset bookings  sunset rate) Tj
T*
(Pony rides  pony rate) Tj
T*
(Private rides  package rate) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Unit economics rule) Tj
T*
(Do not expand products that consistently produce weak contribution margins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8\) Partnership-Led Sales Plan) Tj
T*
(Primary channel: Rosendal accommodation partners.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Give each partner a clear booking/referral process) Tj
T*
(Offer fair referral commissions \(e.g., 10?20% depending on volume\)) Tj
T*
(Focus on same-day response and reliable guest handling) Tj
T*
() Tj
